    "Id": "vehicledef_Lincoln",
    "Name": "Lincoln FST",
    "Details": "Created as a heavily armed fire support vehicle for SLDF use, the 55 ton Lincoln FST was designed to work in tandem with other tanks such as the Washington or Hamilton models. A 165 rated fusion engine allows a maximum speed of 54 kph while 10.5 tons of armor provide sufficient protection. An Artemis-IV enhanced LRM-20 and a pair of Artemis-IV enhanced SRM-6s make up the bulk of the tanks fire power; with a pair of Small Pulse Lasers providing additional fire power at shorter ranges.\n\n<b><color=#ffcc00>Movement: 3/5 hexes / 90/150 meters.</color></b>\n\n<color=#ffcc00><b>Armor:</b> Armor\n<b>Structure:</b> Structure\n<b>Values       A        S  </b>\n<b>Front</b>       155     30\n<b>Left</b>         125     30\n<b>Right</b>       125     30\n<b>Rear</b>         90     30\n<b>Turret</b>      125     30\n\n<b>Total</b>      620    150</color>\n\n<color=#ff0000>Quirk: Main Battle Tank</color>",
